Now understand expected extensionArgs with selectorDir. Tests:

1. selectorDir "/s", no loadExtension, keepExtensions false, headless false -> ["--load-extension=/s"] (adds dev selector but does NOT isolate profile, i.e. no disable-extensions-except).
2. loadExtension /x, keep false, headless false, selectorDir /s -> ["--load-extension=/x,/s", "--disable-extensions-except=/x,/s"].
3. no loadExt, keep false, headless true, selectorDir /s -> ["--load-extension=/s", "--disable-extensions-except=/s"].

Existing without selector:
- loadExt undefined, keep false, headless true -> ["--disable-extensions"]
- loadExt /x -> load + except
- windowed no load -> []
- keep true no load -> []
- keep true load /x -> ["--load-extension=/x"]

Need to implement. Concept: combine loadExtension and selectorDir into list. "isolate" if loadExtension exists OR headless. If selector only in windowed mode, no isolation. That matches.

Pseudo:
```
export function extensionArgs(options: Pick<..., "loadExtension" | "keepExtensions" | "headless" | "selectorDir">): string[] {
  const dirs = [options.loadExtension, options.selectorDir].filter(Boolean) as string[];
  const args: string[] = [];
  if (dirs.length) args.push(`--load-extension=${dirs.join(",")}`);
  if (options.keepExtensions) return args;
  // headless or when run loads a user extension, isolate
  if (options.loadExtension) args.push(`--disable-extensions-except=${dirs.join(",")}`);
  else if (options.headless) {
    if (dirs.length) args.push(`--disable-extensions-except=${dirs.join(",")}`);
    else args.push("--disable-extensions");
  }
  return args;
}
```
Check case headless true, no dirs -> ["--disable-extensions"] ✓. keep true with selector? Not tested. keep returns args just load-extension.

Now resolveDevSelectorDir. Test: root has .output/chrome-mv3 (age 10 → newer) and .output/chrome-mv3-dev (older). Expect newer build chosen by manifest mtime. Also "names a missing one" - test only checks newer one; maybe error message mention. Need find how it should be used and maybe flag `--dev-selector`. Test says "--dev-selector adds Dev Selector without isolating a windowed profile". So likely need parseArgs option too though tests only test extensionArgs directly with selectorDir. But to make coherent source change, add `--dev-selector` flag and use it. Let's inspect open.ts more broadly for extension handling and working dir. Also README maybe describes intended feature? grep found nothing about dev selector in README. Let's search git history? Repo maybe intentionally tasks. Check other tests referencing selectorDir or resolveDevSelectorDir.

